{{> Start this}}

{{> Logo this}}

{{!--
  The first password of an account a master admin created in the Admin
  Dashboard (Users > Create User, #9139; Types/Accounts/SetPasswordLink). The
  admin never makes one up and passes it on: the new user chooses their own
  with this link, which works once and for expiresInDays days, and is spent
  on the same page and endpoint as a password reset link.

  The same email goes to such an account when its owner asks Forgot password
  for a link (#9260). requestedAt is set then (RequestOriginUtil): it says a
  request was made, and when and from where, as a reset email does - anybody
  who knows the address can ask - instead of saying an administrator made
  the account.
--}}

{{> EmailTitle title=(concat "Set your password for " (brandName)) }}

{{#if requestedAt}}
{{> InfoBlock plainInfo=(concat "We received a request to set a password for your " (brandName) " account, " email ". Choose your password to sign in.")}}
{{else}}
{{> InfoBlock plainInfo=(concat "An administrator created a " (brandName) " account for you, " email ". Choose your password to sign in.")}}
{{/if}}

{{> ButtonBlock buttonUrl=tokenVerifyUrl buttonText="Set Your Password"}}

{{> VerticalSpace this}}

{{> LinkBlock linkUrl=tokenVerifyUrl linkLabel="Or copy and paste this link into your browser:"}}

{{> VerticalSpace this}}

{{#if requestedAt}}
{{> InfoBlock info="Details of the request:"}}

{{> DetailBoxStart this }}
{{> DetailBoxField title="Requested at:" plainText=requestedAt }}
{{> RequestOriginFields this }}
{{> DetailBoxEnd this }}
{{/if}}

{{> InfoBlock plainInfo=(concat "The link works once and expires in " expiresInDays " days. If it has expired, ask for a new one with Forgot password on the sign-in page.")}}

{{> InfoBlock plainInfo="Not expecting this? You can safely ignore this email. Without the link above, nobody can set a password for this account."}}

{{> SupportBlock this }}

{{> Footer this}}

{{> End this}}
